@title Booking web tier architecture
@subtitle eu-west-1, owner Booking Platform, reviewed 2026-09-28

## Overview
Customers reach us through CloudFront with a WAF in front. The tier is spread over two Availability Zones so that it survives losing one.

## Diagram
diagram booking dir=LR title="Booking web tier, eu-west-1"
booking: trav "Travelers" user
booking: cf "CloudFront and WAF" ext
booking: alb "Application Load Balancer" lb focus
booking: nata "NAT Gateway A" svc
booking: natb "NAT Gateway B" svc
booking: wa "Web Fleet A" svc "Auto Scaling group"
booking: wb "Web Fleet B" svc "Auto Scaling group"
booking: dbp "Bookings DB Primary" db focus
booking: dbs "Bookings DB Standby" db
booking: s3 "S3 Gateway Endpoint" svc
booking: inv "Partner Inventory API" ext
booking: group psub "Public subnets 10.40.0.0/23" alb, nata, natb
booking: group asub "App subnets 10.40.10.0/23" wa, wb
booking: group dsub "Data subnets 10.40.20.0/23" dbp, dbs
booking: group vpc "Booking VPC 10.40.0.0/16" psub, asub, dsub, s3
booking: group acct "Booking account" vpc
booking: trav -> cf : HTTPS
booking: cf -> alb : origin request
booking: alb -> wa : port 8080
booking: alb -> wb : port 8080
booking: wa -> dbp : SQL
booking: wb -> dbp : SQL
booking: dbp -> dbs : synchronous replication
booking: wa -> nata : outbound
booking: nata -> inv : HTTPS
booking: wb -> s3 : receipts

## Capacity
table = component,size,scaling; Web fleets,m6i.large,3 to 12 instances per AZ on CPU above 55%; Bookings DB,db.r6g.2xlarge Multi-AZ,storage autoscaling to 4 TB; NAT gateways,one per AZ,5 Gbps each
